{
  "id": "hemodynamic-response",
  "term": "hemodynamic response",
  "definition": "Hemodynamic response is the pattern of blood-related changes linked to brain activity, such as shifts in oxygenated and deoxygenated hemoglobin that can be measured with methods like fNIRS. In this context, it refers to how blood flow and oxygenation change in and around brain areas during a task, while also being vulnerable to non-brain influences such as extracerebral blood flow.",
